## Run Locally

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/DARSHAN-debug777/autonomous-resource-collection-rl.git
cd autonomous-resource-collection-rl
```

Install dependencies:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

Launch the application:

```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

## Limitations

- The Q-Learning agent uses a tabular representation rather than a neural network.
- Its state representation is approximate and does not include the complete future resource sequence.
- Optimal Knapsack is an offline benchmark with access to all resources, while Q-Learning makes sequential decisions.

## Future Improvements

- Improve Q-Learning performance through controlled experiments.
- Investigate richer state representations.
- Compare different exploration strategies.
- Analyse generalisation across unseen resource distributions.

